[h1]Keep the right amount — in stacks your pawns can actually use[/h1]

Storage Group Quotas adds [b]per-item limits[/b] to vanilla storage groups. Linked shelves are counted together as one group.

It is especially useful for ammo depots: instead of one huge pile that everyone may wait to reserve, you can keep several real stacks as separate pickup targets.

The quota list uses a familiar category tree. Set one value for a broad category, refine it on a child category, and override only the exceptional items.

[h2]Choose the mode you need[/h2]
• [b]Entire storage count[/b] — Keep no more than X of each item type in this group. Best for medicine, meals, shells, and anything where only the total matters.

• [b]Similar stacks ×N[/b] — Keep at most X items per stack and at most N physical stacks. For example, 25 × 4 gives a total capacity of 100 across up to four stacks.

New quota settings start at N = 1; existing settings keep their saved N. The quota tree refreshes with the vanilla allowed-item list while open, and both windows share category folding.

With some hauling or reservation optimization mods, one physical stack may be reserved by only one pawn or job at a time. Multiple stacks provide separate reservation targets and can reduce queues when several weapons reload or are resupplied together.

[h2]What happens to excess items?[/h2]
• Incoming hauling respects the group's remaining quota.

• Existing excess is moved by normal hauling jobs — never deleted or teleported.

• Haulers first use valid storage outside the group. If none exists, they place the excess on a reachable floor cell outside the group.

• In Similar stacks mode, haulers first try to split or consolidate stacks inside the group. Anything that cannot fit the selected layout is moved outside.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
Select a shelf or stockpile → open [b]Storage[/b] → click [b]Quotas[/b] → choose a mode and set the global default. Expand the tree to set a category or individual item; unset children inherit the nearest configured parent.

[b]Important:[/b] a category value is calculated separately for every descendant item; it is not one shared total for the whole category. In Entire storage mode, 0 means unlimited. In Similar stacks mode, 0 uses that item's current stack limit. The mod does not change ThingDef.stackLimit globally.

[h2]Requirements and compatibility[/h2]
• RimWorld 1.6

• [b]Requires Harmony[/b]

• Works with Combat Extended ammunition; Combat Extended is not required

• Optional Pick Up And Haul destination-capacity support

• [b]Incompatible with Stack Gap[/b] — disable it first; its settings are not migrated

[url=https://github.com/Steel-Shadow/RimWorld-StorageGroupQuotas]Source code, full documentation, and issue tracker[/url]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]存得刚刚好，也让 Pawn 真正取用得到[/h1]

Storage Group Quotas（存储组配额）为原版存储组增加[b]按物品分别计算的数量上限[/b]。链接在一起的货架会作为一个整体统计。

它尤其适合弹药库：与其让所有 Pawn 等待同一个可能已被预留的大堆，不如保留多个真实堆栈，提供彼此独立的取用目标。

配额列表采用熟悉的分类树：可以先给大类设置一个值，再在子类中细分，只覆盖少数例外物品。

[h2]选择需要的模式[/h2]
• [b]整个仓库数量[/b] — 该组内每种物品最多保留 X 件。适合药品、食物、炮弹等只关心总数的物品。

• [b]类似堆栈 ×N[/b] — 每堆最多 X 件，最多保留 N 个真实堆栈。例如 25 × 4 表示最多四堆、总容量 100。

新建配额设置从 N = 1 开始；已有设置保留已保存的 N。配额树在窗口打开期间会随原版允许物品列表刷新，两个窗口也会共享分类折叠状态。

在部分搬运或预留优化模组下，一堆实体物品同时可能只能被一个 Pawn 或任务预留。多个堆栈能提供彼此独立的预留目标，减少多件武器同时换弹或补给时的排队。

[h2]超量物品会去哪？[/h2]
• 新的入库搬运不会超过存储组的剩余配额。

• 已经超量的物品会由 Pawn 通过正常搬运移走，不会被删除或瞬移。

• 搬运工会优先送到该组之外的合法仓储；没有可用仓储时，则放到该组外可到达的地面。

• 在“类似堆栈 ×N”模式中，搬运工会先尝试在组内拆分或归并；无法纳入所选布局的部分会移到组外。

[h2]使用方法[/h2]
选择货架或仓储区 → 打开[b]存储[/b]标签 → 点击[b]存储配额[/b] → 选择模式并设置全局默认值。展开分类树后可设置分类或单个物品；未设置的子项会继承最近的父级。

[b]请注意：[/b]分类值会由每种后代物品分别计算，并不是整个分类共用一个总额。“整个仓库数量”模式下，0 表示不限；“类似堆栈 ×N”模式下，0 表示使用该物品当前的堆叠上限。本模组不会全局修改 ThingDef.stackLimit。

[h2]需求与兼容[/h2]
• RimWorld 1.6

• [b]需要 Harmony[/b]

• 可用于 Combat Extended 弹药，但不强制依赖 CE

• 为 Pick Up And Haul 提供可选的目标容量适配

• [b]与 Stack Gap 不兼容[/b] — 请先禁用；旧配置不会迁移

[url=https://github.com/Steel-Shadow/RimWorld-StorageGroupQuotas]源代码、完整说明与问题反馈[/url]
